ion i have done at least  one active shooter situation since first  grade  did that active shooter training you  underwent from  first grade through high school kick in  it did  immediately no one should ever have to  experience what happened that monday  it's the reality of the day we live in  and  it won't be the last time that it will  happen sadly  you know at the end of our interview he  told us that when he comes back to work  here at the grocery store and he expects  to  he expects that kroger which owns the  grocery store is going to provide an  armed security guard  at all times anthony he told us he's a  gun owner and he also said this he said  david i would appreciate the right to  actually bring my weapon which i'm  licensed to carry here to work and have  it on me  because he said after what i lived  through i'd like the ability to protect  myself  and people around me just a surreal  description of what happened in that  supermarket  david thank you
 

